.TH SETIMEX 1.SH NAMEsetimex \- check and set the system clock.SH SYNOPSIS\fBsetimex\fR[options].SH DESCRIPTION\fBsetimex\fRchecks the system clock and sets it: outright to a date given, or onlyif the old one looks wrong.  DESIGNA VLT, UTIL 2.80..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-s=\fIdate\fRset this date..TP 12\fB\-d=\fIdate\fRset this date only if the current one is wrong..TP 12\fB\-1, +1\fRput the clock back or forward an hour..TP 12\fB\-s\fRrun OS-9's own\fBsetime \-s\fR.\fR.TP 12\fB\-t\fRtest: set a wrong time and correct it at once..TP 12\fB\-x\fRexit 0 if the time was right, 1 if not;\fB\-e\fRthe reverse;\fB\-n\fRalways 0, the default..TP 12\fB\-0\fRdebugging output..PPA date is\fIYYYYMMDDhhmmss\fR,\fR\fIYYMMDDhhmmss\fR,\fR\fIYYMMDDhhmm\fRor\fIYYMMDD\fR,\fRor the same with a three-digit year..SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fRUnder os9exec the clock cannot be set; see\fBsetime\fR.\fR.SH SEE ALSOsetime